 "insights": [
  "Real GDP grew 4.6% in 2025, broadly unchanged from 4.7% a year earlier (2010\u201319 average: 5.0%).",
  "Inflation was 4.1% in 2025, inside the Central Bank of Kenya's 5% \u00b1 2.5 target band.",
  "Services is the largest sector at 55% of GDP; agriculture still contributes 23%.",
  "Kenya is the #1 economy in the EAC, with 33% of the bloc's output.",
  "Growth was faster than 55% of African economies (Africa median: 4.5%)."
 ],
 "considerations": [
  "Imports (22% of GDP) exceed exports (16%): export diversification and value addition would ease external-balance pressure.",
  "Remittances (3.8% of GDP) are a key foreign-exchange source; lowering transfer costs supports household incomes.",
  "Raising agricultural productivity matters for both growth and food-price inflation.",
  "Regional infrastructure links (roads, rail, power) deepen EAC trade where Kenya is the largest economy."
 ]
